 "_about": "T3.7 hand-made and Azure-made: per lab family, a resource a learner might add by hand of a type the diagram knows and one of a type it does not (an unknown type that names a subnet: Redis Enterprise's subnetId, an App Service's virtualNetworkSubnetId), grafted onto that family lab's own rows; and one row per AZURE_MADE pattern. Shapes from Learn's REST references (networkSecurityGroups, publicIPAddresses, localNetworkGateways, storageAccounts, disks, actionGroups, redisEnterprise, Web/sites, expressRouteCircuits, Search searchServices, availabilitySets, Automation automationAccounts). Fake subscription, TEST-NET addresses. A group is Azure's only when a row in the same graph says so (a cluster's nodeResourceGroup, an environment's infrastructureResourceGroup, or the group's own managedBy): azureGroups holds the group rows that name the groups the azureMade rows sit in.",
